[
    {
        "text": "We use some cryptography which involves the transformation of data for the purposes of secure communication. Even if an adversary intercepts a message from Alice to Bob, they won't be able to decipher it without a special key. Something like the Veneer cipher is what we call symmetric encryption. For example, we can use the key HODL to transform our plaintext into ciphertext. It's not impossible, but it'll be time consuming for an adversary to figure out what the plaintext is without knowing the key. However, if we give someone the key we use to encrypt the message, they can use it to decrypt it. That's why it's symmetric. The same key is used to encrypt and decrypt.",
        "start": 240,
        "end": 41020,
        "confidence": 0.98092663,
        "channel": null,
